Now the big one: RaceServiceImpl. Changes:

1. Imports: RegisterWithdrawalRequest, RevokeWithdrawalRequest, RunnerStatusResponse, WithdrawalListResponse, WithdrawalResponse, WithdrawalStatus, WithdrawalRow, ResultEntryResponse (for runner status — actually I'll build RunnerStatusResponse from ResultEntry).
2. submitTiming: guard active withdrawal → 409.
3. reviseTime: guard active withdrawal → 409.
4. addPenalty: guard ADD_TIME on withdrawn runner → 409.
5. sealRace: pass withdrawals to ResultCalculator.compute; snapshot entries include lastCheckpointCode.
6. getResults: pass withdrawals to liveStanding.
7. New methods: registerWithdrawal, revokeWithdrawal, getWithdrawals, getRunnerStatus.

For getRunnerStatus: compute standing entries (live or snapshot) and find entry for bib; attach latest withdrawal. For live: use ResultCalculator directly. For sealed: snapshot entries. Let me write:

```java
@Override
@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public RunnerStatusResponse getRunnerStatus(String raceId, String bib) {
    RaceRow race = repository.findRace(raceId)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new NotFoundException("赛事不存在: " + raceId));
    RunnerRow runner = repository.findRunner(raceId, bib)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new NotFoundException("选手不存在: " + bib));
    WithdrawalRow latest = repository.findLatestWithdrawal(raceId, bib).orElse(null);
    WithdrawalResponse withdrawalResponse = latest == null ? null : ResponseMapper.toWithdrawalResponse(latest);
    if (race.status() == RaceStatus.SEALED) {
        SnapshotRow snapshot = repository.findSnapshot(raceId).orElseThrow(...);
        SnapshotEntryRow entry = snapshot.entries().stream().filter(e -> e.bib().equals(bib)).findFirst()
                .orElseThrow(...); // runner exists so entry exists
        return new RunnerStatusResponse(raceId, bib, entry.status(), entry.finishTimeMs(),
                entry.lastCheckpointCode(), entry.missingCheckpoints(), withdrawalResponse);
    }
    List<ResultEntry> entries = ResultCalculator.compute(
            List.of(runner), repository.findPenalties(raceId), repository.findCheckpoints(raceId),
            repository.findTimingsForRunner(raceId, bib), repository.findWithdrawals(raceId));
    ResultEntry entry = entries.getFirst();
    return new RunnerStatusResponse(raceId, bib, entry.status(), entry.finishTimeMs(),
            entry.lastCheckpointCode(), entry.missingCheckpoints(), withdrawalResponse);
}
```

Wait — ResultCalculator.compute with only this runner's timings: findTimingsForRunner gives this runner's timings; penalties for the whole race filtered by bib inside. Withdrawals for race filtered by bib. Good — compute with single-runner list works.

registerWithdrawal:

```java
@Override
@Transactional
public ServiceResult registerWithdrawal(String raceId, RegisterWithdrawalRequest request) {
    return withIdempotency(request.requestId(), "REGISTER_WITHDRAWAL",
            orderedParams(
                    "raceId", raceId,
                    "withdrawalKey", request.withdrawalKey(),
                    "bib", request.bib(),
                    "status", request.status(),
                    "reason", request.reason(),
                    "lastPassedCheckpoint", request.lastPassedCheckpoint(),
                    "expectedVersion", request.expectedVersion()),
            () -> {
                // withdrawalKey 是第二层全局幂等键：同参重放原结果，异参409。
                WithdrawalRow existing = repository.findWithdrawal(request.withdrawalKey()).orElse(null);
                if (existing != null) {
                    return replayWithdrawalOrConflict(raceId, request, existing);
                }
                RaceRow race = requireOpenRace(raceId, request.expectedVersion());
                RunnerRow runner = requireRunner(raceId, request.bib());
                WithdrawalStatus status = parseWithdrawalStatus(request.status());
                String reason = request.reason() == null ? null : request.reason().trim();
                if (reason == null || reason.isEmpty()) {
                    throw new BadRequestException("退赛原因不能为空");
                }
                // 已取消资格或已有完赛计时的选手禁止登记退赛。
                boolean disqualified = repository.findPenalties(raceId).stream()
                        .anyMatch(p -> p.bib().equals(request.bib())
                                && p.type() == PenaltyType.DISQUALIFY && !p.revoked());
                if (disqualified) {
                    throw new ConflictException("选手已取消资格，禁止登记退赛: " + request.bib());
                }
                if (runner.finishTimeMs() != null) {
                    throw new ConflictException("选手已有完赛计时，禁止登记退赛: " + request.bib());
                }
                // 同选手已有生效退赛登记：同状态按幂等返回首次结果，DNS/DNF 相互改写409。
                WithdrawalRow active = repository.findActiveWithdrawal(raceId, request.bib()).orElse(null);
                List<CheckpointTimingRow> timings = repository.findTimingsForRunner(raceId, request.bib());
                String lastCheckpointCode = validateWithdrawalPreconditions(status, request, timings);
                if (active != null) {
                    if (active.status() != status) {
                        throw new ConflictException("DNS 与 DNF 不允许相互改写: " + request.bib());
                    }
                    throw new ConflictException("选手已登记退赛: " + request.bib());
                }
                ...
            });
}
```

Hmm wait — "同状态重复登记按幂等返回首次结果". With a *different* withdrawalKey but same status? Re-read: "同状态重复登记按幂等返回首次结果，DNS 与 DNF 相互改写一律409". 

Interpretation: if a runner already has an active DNS withdrawal and another registration for DNS comes in (different withdrawalKey), return the first result idempotently (the first withdrawal record). If DNF comes in → 409.

Hmm, but is that "幂等"? Returning the first registration's response for a different withdrawalKey... The spec says "同状态重复登记按幂等返回首次结果" — yes, return the first result. So: active withdrawal exists with same status → return ServiceResult.created(toWithdrawalResponse(active))? But the response of the first registration was 201 with the first withdrawal row. Return that. But what if the reason differs? Spec doesn't distinguish; "同状态重复登记按幂等返回首次结果" — same status → return first result regardless. I'll implement: active with same status → return first withdrawal record (201). Active with different status → 409.

Hmm, but wait — should same-status duplicate also require same checkpoint for DNF? "同状态重复登记按幂等返回首次结果" is unconditional. Keep it simple: same status → return first result.

But careful with ordering of validations: if the new request would fail validation (e.g. DNS but runner has timings — impossible if active DNS exists since timings can't be added after withdrawal... actually timings can't be added after withdrawal, and withdrawal requires no timings for DNS. So state can't change underneath). For an active DNF, runner still has no finish time (can't revise after withdrawal). So if active withdrawal exists, the preconditions that held at registration still hold. So check active withdrawal BEFORE other validations? But disqualified check: a DISQUALIFY penalty could be added after withdrawal (allowed). Then a duplicate registration would hit "disqualified → 409" instead of idempotent replay. Edge case; order matters little. I'll check active withdrawal first (idempotent replay semantics take precedence), then 409 checks (DQ, finish time), then 422 validations.

Actually wait — order between "active withdrawal replay" and version check (requireOpenRace)? The replay of first result shouldn't require version match... Hmm. The first result was a success at some version. "同状态重复登记按幂等返回首次结果" — return first result. If expectedVersion doesn't match current, is it still a replay? For the withdrawalKey-level replay (same key), submitTiming's pattern checks existing timing BEFORE requireOpenRace — replay happens regardless of version. I'll follow the same pattern: withdrawalKey replay first, then active-withdrawal same-status replay... hmm, but the active-withdrawal replay needs the race to exist and be open? If race is sealed, registration is prohibited (409). But duplicate registration after seal — "封榜后禁止新增或撤销退赛" → 409. So requireOpenRace must come before the active-withdrawal replay. Order:

1. withdrawalKey exists → replay or 409 (before race checks, like submitTiming).
2. requireOpenRace (404/409 sealed/version).
3. requireRunner (404).
4. parse status (400), reason (400).
5. active withdrawal: same status → return first result (201); different status → 409.
6. DQ → 409; finish time → 409.
7. DNS/DNF precondition validation → 422/400.
8. bumpVersion, insert, return 201.

For step 5, response status: first registration returned 201. Return created(toWithdrawalResponse(active)).

Hmm, one subtlety: the idempotency record (requestId layer) will store THIS request's response (the replayed first result) under the new requestId. That's consistent with withIdempotency semantics.

validateWithdrawalPreconditions:

```java
private String validateWithdrawalPreconditions(WithdrawalStatus status, RegisterWithdrawalRequest request, List<CheckpointTimingRow> timings) {
    if (status == WithdrawalStatus.DNS) {
        if (request.lastPassedCheckpoint() != null) {
            throw new BadRequestException("DNS 不得携带 lastPassedCheckpoint");
        }
        if (!timings.isEmpty()) {
            throw new UnprocessableEntityException("DNS 要求该选手尚无任何分段记录");
        }
        return null;
    }
    // DNF
    if (request.lastPassedCheckpoint() == null || request.lastPassedCheckpoint().isBlank()) {
        throw new BadRequestException("DNF 必须携带 lastPassedCheckpoint");
    }
    if (timings.isEmpty()) {
        throw new UnprocessableEntityException("DNF 要求该选手已有至少一条分段记录");
    }
    CheckpointTimingRow last = timings.getLast(); // ordered by position
    if (!last.checkpointCode().equals(request.lastPassedCheckpoint())) {
        throw new UnprocessableEntityException("lastPassedCheckpoint 须为已有分段记录中顺序最大者: " + last.checkpointCode());
    }
    return last.checkpointCode();
}
```

findTimingsForRunner orders by position, so getLast() is max position. Good.

revokeWithdrawal:

```java
@Override
@Transactional
public ServiceResult revokeWithdrawal(String raceId, String withdrawalKey, RevokeWithdrawalRequest request) {
    return withIdempotency(request.requestId(), "REVOKE_WITHDRAWAL",
            orderedParams(
                    "raceId", raceId,
                    "withdrawalKey", withdrawalKey,
                    "expectedVersion", request.expectedVersion()),
            () -> {
                RaceRow race = requireOpenRace(raceId, request.expectedVersion());
                WithdrawalRow withdrawal = repository.findWithdrawal(withdrawalKey)
                        .orElseThrow(() -> new NotFoundException("退赛登记不存在: " + withdrawalKey));
                if (!withdrawal.raceId().equals(raceId)) {
                    throw new NotFoundException("退赛登记不属于该赛事: " + withdrawalKey);
                }
                if (withdrawal.revoked()) {
                    throw new ConflictException("退赛登记已撤销: " + withdrawalKey);
                }
                long now = clock.millis();
                bumpVersion(race, request.expectedVersion());
                int updated = repository.markWithdrawalRevoked(withdrawalKey, now);
                if (updated == 0) {
                    throw new ConflictException("退赛登记已撤销: " + withdrawalKey);
                }
                WithdrawalRow refreshed = repository.findWithdrawal(withdrawalKey).orElseThrow();
                return ServiceResult.ok(ResponseMapper.toWithdrawalResponse(refreshed));
            });
}
```

