replayWithdrawalOrConflict:

```java
private ServiceResult replayWithdrawalOrConflict(
        String raceId, RegisterWithdrawalRequest request, WithdrawalRow existing) {
    boolean sameParams = existing.raceId().equals(raceId)
            && existing.bib().equals(request.bib())
            && existing.status().name().equals(request.status())
            && existing.reason().equals(request.reason())
            && java.util.Objects.equals(existing.lastCheckpointCode(), request.lastPassedCheckpoint());
    if (!sameParams) {
        throw new ConflictException("withdrawalKey 已用于不同参数的退赛登记: " + request.withdrawalKey());
    }
    return ServiceResult.created(ResponseMapper.toWithdrawalResponse(existing));
}
```

Note: status param comparison — request.status() is a String like "DNS". Compare with name(). But if request.status() is "dns" lowercase? parseWithdrawalStatus uses valueOf — invalid → 400. For replay comparison, exact string match is fine (different case → different params → 409; acceptable).

Also reason: stored reason is the raw request reason (I trim only for blank check? If I trim for storage, replay comparison must compare trimmed). Simpler: store the reason as-is, validate non-blank via trim check. Compare raw. OK — store request.reason() as-is.

parseWithdrawalStatus:
```java
private static WithdrawalStatus parseWithdrawalStatus(String status) {
    try {
        return WithdrawalStatus.valueOf(status);
    } catch (IllegalArgumentException ex) {
        throw new BadRequestException("未知退赛状态: " + status);
    }
}
```

requireNoActiveWithdrawal helper:
```java
private void requireNoActiveWithdrawal(String raceId, String bib, String operation) {
    if (repository.findActiveWithdrawal(raceId, bib).isPresent()) {
        throw new ConflictException("选手已登记退赛，禁止" + operation + ": " + bib);
    }
}
